# Infinity Protocol Testing Standards v3.0

## 1. The Separation of Concerns
- **Vitest**: Used exclusively for Unit Testing and Component Testing (non-browser logic).
- **Playwright**: Used exclusively for E2E Testing, complete user flows, and browser-dependent interactions.

## 2. When to Test
Testing is a first-class citizen in the Infinity Protocol. Do NOT skip testing for:
- **Authentication Flows**: Login, Registration, JWT state.
- **Financial/Checkout**: Payment calculation, Cart adjustments, Stripe webhooks.
- **Database Mutators**: Any logic writing to Firestore or Firebase Functions.

## 3. Unit Testing (Vitest)
- Place tests adjacent to the file being tested (e.g., `calculateTotal.ts` -> `calculateTotal.test.ts`).
- Mock all external dependencies (Firebase, Stripe, etc.). Use `vi.mock()`.
- Keep component tests focused on rendering and local state, NOT full page routing.

## 4. E2E Testing (Playwright)
- Place tests in the `/e2e` directory at the project root.
- Treat the application as a black box. Avoid mocking where possible; prefer hitting an emulator or a dedicated staging database.
- Name tests clearly describing the user intent: `user-can-complete-checkout.spec.ts`.
- Use `data-testid` attributes on elements to ensure brittle CSS changes do not break tests.

## 5. Mocking Firebase (The Protocol Way)
- When using Playwright, always point the app to the Firebase Local Emulator Suite if executing locally or in CI.
- When using Vitest, use `vitest-mock-extended` or standard `vi.mock('firebase/firestore')` to intercept UI interactions.

## 7. Visual Testing (Playwright Snapshots)
- Use `await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot()` to catch UI regressions on premium "Liquid Glass" components.
- Always name snapshots descriptively: `toHaveScreenshot('user-profile-header-dark.png')`.
- Maintain snapshots in the repository; commit changes only after manual verification of the delta.

## 8. Continuous Integration
- All critical paths MUST have an E2E test verifying success and standard failure modes before a branch is merged into `main`.
- Failing tests absolutely block deployments. Do not bypass the Safe-Deploy guards.

## 9. Security Rules Testing
- All Firestore/Storage rules MUST have dedicated unit tests in `__tests__/security/`.
- Use `@firebase/rules-unit-testing` to verify both `assertSucceeds` (authorized access) and `assertFails` (unauthorized access).
- Rules testing is mandatory for any project handling User Data or Payment information.

## 10. Accessibility (A11y) Audits
- Automated A11y scans using `axe-playwright` are required for all public-facing pages.
- Zero violations is the standard. Use `expect(accessibilityScanResults.violations).toEqual([])`.

## 11. Performance Budgets (Liquid Smooth UX)
- Use Playwright timing audits to ensure main pages load within 2 seconds.
- Monitor `LCP` (Largest Contentful Paint) and `TBT` (Total Blocking Time) during E2E flows.
- Performance regressions on premium animated sections must be treated as critical bugs.

## 12. API Contract & Data Integrity
- Use Zod schemas to validate all data flowing between Frontend and Firebase/APIs.
- Maintain unit tests in `__tests__/integrity/` to verify schema compliance.
- No ad-hoc `any` types for data payloads; strict schema enforcement is mandatory.

## 13. Omni-Sentinel & Living Documentation
- Every project must maintain a `TEST_INDEX.md` as a living registry of its testing surface area.
- Rule drift is strictly prohibited. Use `dv fix-drift` to auto-heal project alignment with the Master protocol.
- Parallelized testing via `dv test-all` is the standard for workspace-wide validation.

## 14. Neural Sentinel & AI-Context
- `AI_DEBUG.md` must be maintained as an immutable persistence layer for architectural decisions.
- Project fingerprinting must be updated whenever new core technologies (e.g. Edge, RTDB) are integrated.
- Real-time telemetry via `dv log` is the primary mechanism for workspace-wide health monitoring.
- CI workflows must remain pinned to the Master template via `dv sync-ci`.

## 15. Resilience & Chaos Engineering
- All E2E suites must include chaos testing (latency, network failure) to ensure frontend robustness.
- Error boundaries and fallback states must be verified under simulated API downtime.
- Performance budgets are strictly enforced: <2000ms page load is a hard requirement.

## 16. Sovereign Governance
- All projects must adhere to the Master Ruleset version pinned in `SOVEREIGN_LOCK`.
- Workspace dependencies must be mapped via `dv graph` to monitor integration risks.
- The `dv dash` hub is the single source of truth for workspace-wide health and sanity checks.

